Aether: ads and Pocket out

GIFFT bridge, MaRS ads, Pocket data and rest, manual updates, viaduct/necko, crash ping, GIFFT leftovers.

Squashed from 8 units:

  [core/72-gifft-bridge.patch]
  Aether: remove the GIFFT timing-distribution bridge
  
  Remove the GIFFT bridge: the Rust-to-C++ FFI that forwarded
  timing-distribution samples to the legacy backend. The C++ shells were
  already no-ops; now the callers go too:
  
  - glean/api timing_distribution.rs + labeled_timing_distribution.rs:
    drop every extern GIFFT block and unsafe call (start, stop,
    cancel, accumulate x3, both files). Profiler markers stay (local
    only), as do the IPC paths, the metric-id plumbing and the
    gifft_time_unit fields/signatures consumed by generated code.
  - glean/bindings TimingDistribution.cpp: delete the 9 no-op
    GIFFT_TimingDistribution* / GIFFT_LabeledTimingDistribution*
    functions. The live Standalone/binding code below is untouched.
  
  [core/73-mars-ads.patch]
  Aether: delete the MARS ads stack
  
  Delete the MARS (Mozilla Ad Routing Service) stack instead of
  leaving it pref-gated. Nothing fetched through it by default, but
  dead code that phones home has no place in the tree:
  
  - Delete AdsFeed.sys.mjs, AdsClient.sys.mjs and the generated
    RustAdsClient.sys.mjs (3734 lines), plus the ads-client dep from
    gkrust-uniffi-components, its config.toml section and its moz.build
    entry.
  - Delete the NewTabAttribution feed/service/actors (click/impression
    attribution exists only for ads) and their tests.
  - DiscoveryStreamFeed: drop the AdsClient/RustAdsClient imports,
    _fetchSpocsWithAdsClient, the placement getters, the MARS branches
    in loadSpocs/normalize/ranking/cache/clearSpocs/block-reporting and
    the contextual-ads getter.
  - TopSitesFeed: drop the MARS/Contile dual path (Contile path stays),
    _fetchSitesWithAdsClient, _normalizeTileData, the adsClient member
    and the unifiedAds prefs/cases.
  - PlacesFeed: drop the MARS blocklist reporting.
  - ActivityStream: drop the adsfeed registration, the unifiedAds and
    contextual-ads prefs and helpers. Reducers/Actions: drop the Ads
    state slice and action types.
  - firefox.js: drop the unifiedAds defaults. Tests: drop the ads
    xpcshell modules, the contextual-ads test and the AdsClient MARS
    test.
  
  Left for follow-ups: sponsored-toggles UI (now inert), jest/browser
  tests referencing removed prefs, content-src ad components, and the
  Pocket/weather/stocks remote feeds (their own units).
  
  [core/74-pocket-data.patch]
  Aether: delete the Pocket data path from newtab
  
  Delete the Pocket data path from newtab: stories and sponsored
  content no longer exist as a concept in the tree.
  
  - Delete DiscoveryStreamFeed.sys.mjs and TopStoriesFeed.sys.mjs, their
    ActivityStream registrations/imports, and the Ads redux leftovers
    from 73 (state slice, reducer, action types).
  - ActivityStream: drop ~30 pocket/spoc/placement/contextual prefs,
    the showSpocs helper, the contextual-ads helper and the topstories
    section order entry.
  - SectionsManager: drop the topstories built-in section descriptor.
  - StartupCacheInit: drop the spocs startup-cache reply path.
  - PrefsFeed: drop the pocket experiment wiring, adsBackend feature
    plumbing and spoc/topstories pref defaults.
  - PlacesFeed: drop the MARS blocklist reporting and the pocket
    reader-URL branch.
  - AboutPreferences: drop the topstories/support-firefox home sections
    (legacy XUL descriptors, Settings and SRD groups) and the
    support-firefox checkbox sync; drop home.inc.xhtml placeholders.
  - firefox.js + preferences.ftl: drop pocket/spoc/sponsored prefs and
    strings. NewTabAttribution feed/service/actors and their tests go
    with the ads stack they served.
  - Tests: drop ads/attribution/contextual xpcshell modules and the
    discovery browser tests + manifest entries.
  
  Kept on purpose for follow-ups: Reducers store shape (content bundle
  reads it), the pocketNewtab Nimbus feature (kept Contile code reads
  some variables), activation-window temp-pref juggling (shared with
  topsites), sponsored-toggles UI strings in content, jest/browser
  tests referencing removed prefs, and the non-WebRTC media recorders.
  
  [core/75-pocket-rest.patch]
  Aether: delete the remaining Pocket surface
  
  Finish the Pocket elimination: remove everything the data-path
  patch (74) left behind.
  
  - TopSitesFeed: resolve Nimbus pocketNewtab reads to constants,
    drop fetchDiscoveryStreamSpocs and Pocket comments.
  - Delete the pocketNewtab, newtabSponsoredContent and adsBackend
    Nimbus features (zero readers left) and the generate-script
    allowlist entry. Generated manifests rebuild from the yaml.
  - Policies: drop the Pocket/Stories/Sponsored branches, the
    already-deprecated DisablePocket policy and schema.
  - SectionsManager/PlacesFeed/NewTabUtils/contentrelevancy: drop the
    pocket context-menu block, block IDs, reader branch and input
    option.
  - UITour: drop pocket tour docs + test.
  
  Also restores the region-basic-config default in firefox.js: the
  region-basic-layout reader needs it and throws without a default,
  which left newtab blank (caught by user testing).
  
  Kept on purpose: Reducers store shape (content bundle reads it),
  activation-window temp-pref juggling (shared with topsites),
  Contile display prefs, content-src components + bundle, jest tests,
  and newtab.ftl story strings (content wave next).
  
  [core/76-manual-updates.patch]
  Aether: manual-only updates, no background checks
  
  Manual-only updates, as agreed: the browser never talks to the
  update server unless the user presses the update button.
  
  - UpdateService manualUpdateOnly is now unconditionally true. That
    early-outs background checks, automatic downloads and the
    background update tasks, while the foreground check behind the
    user-facing button keeps working.
  - ASRouter CheckBrowserNeedsUpdate targeting query no longer fires a
    foreground update check on its own; it reports no pending update.
  
  [core/77-viaduct-necko.patch]
  Aether: remove the viaduct-necko backend
  
  Remove the viaduct-necko HTTP backend: with the MARS/Pocket
  callers gone and Glean upload faking success without I/O, nothing
  can send through it anymore.
  
  - shared/lib.rs + Cargo.toml: drop the viaduct/viaduct-necko deps
    and the backend init in GkRust_Init.
  - Delete services/.../viaduct-necko entirely (backend.cpp/h,
    lib.rs, moz.build, tests) and its services/moz.build entry.
  - Delete the generated RustViaduct.sys.mjs binding + moz.build
    entry (zero importers).
  - Cargo.lock: drop the gkrust-shared edges and the stanza.
  
  The generic viaduct crate stays (other app-services crates link
  it), as does the megazord edge.
  
  [core/78-crash-ping.patch]
  Aether: remove the Glean crash ping
  
  Remove the Glean crash ping end to end.
  
  The crash ping was the last telemetry path with a hardcoded server URL
  (`https://incoming.telemetry.mozilla.org`, hardcoded in the crashping
  crate) and the only one that ran its own HTTP stack outside Glean's
  uploader: the crashreporter client linked `glean` directly and spawned
  `--send-ping` to submit pings, so the uploader cap did not cover it.
  Enabling it was governed by `datareporting.healthreport.uploadEnabled`,
  which already defaults to false here -- but the code that would have
  sent stayed. It does not now.
  
  - Delete the `crashping` crate (its endpoint, ping definitions, metric
    generator and the `crash-ping-metrics` mach command) and the Android
    `crashtools` JNI export that was its other user.
  - Crashreporter client: drop the crashping/glean deps, `--send-ping` /
    `--ping-cleanup`, and the ping send in `ReportCrash::run`. The client
    no longer links Glean at all.
  - CrashManager: drop `sendGleanPing`, `cleanupPings`,
    `sendUnsubmittedPings`, `_sendCrashPing`, `isPingAllowed` and the
    `pingPending` / `setPingSubmitted` store bookkeeping. Crashes are
    still recorded, pruned and aggregated; they just go nowhere.
  - `gen_CrashManager.py`: no longer generates the process ping table.
  - Docs: remove the crash ping lifecycle page and its toctree entry.
  
  `crashreporter.submitReport` / `crashreporter.autoSubmit` (the
  user-consented crash *report*) are untouched and keep working.
  
  [core/79-gifft-leftovers.patch]
  Aether: drop the GIFFT leftovers and the docs of dead telemetry
  
  Drop the GIFFT leftovers and the docs that describe code we
  already deleted.
  
  The GIFFT bridge is gone: the JS side (ExternGlean/InternalGlean) went
  with the marker bridge, and GleanMetric.h no longer mentions
  telemetry_mirror, WithMirror or the GIFFT maps. What was left were four
  headers nothing in the build includes, the probe-scraper's template that
  emits them, and a pile of prose.
  
  - Delete EventGIFFTMap.h, HistogramGIFFTMap.h, ScalarGIFFTMap.h and
    GIFFT.Fwd.h plus their EXPORTS entries.
  - Delete the GIFFT tests (xpcshell, browser, pytest) and their manifest
    entries. test_GIFFT.js drove the removed JS bridge.
  - Delete gifft.md plus the glean_for_legacy_{events,scalars}.md pair --
    all three exist to explain mirroring Glean metrics onto legacy probes
    declared in Histograms.json / Scalars.yaml / Events.yaml, none of
    which exist any more. Fix the eight cross-references to them in
    metric_ids.md, new_metric_types.md, preferences.md, getting_started.md,
    instrumentation_tests.md, and the obsolete telemetry docs.
  - Delete devtools' telemetry.md for the same reason: it walks through
    adding a probe to those three files. Note in devtools/client/shared/
    telemetry.js that reporting is disabled instead -- the module already
    returns null from getChartsFromToolId().
  - Drop the docs/config.yml warning suppression for install-ping.md, a
    file that does not exist.
  - Drop the gifft.html link from translate_events.py's output.
  
  The probe-scraper's gifft_map generator stays: it is tooling for
  `mach glean`, not something the build ships, and it cannot run without
  the legacy probe declaration files either way. Same for `mach gifft`
  and `mach event-into-legacy`.
